     "4m^{2} – 7mn + 3n^{2} + m – n =\nA. (m – n)(4m – 3n + 1).\nB. (m – n)(4m + 3n + 1).\nC. (m + n)(4m – 3n – 1).\nD. (m + n)(4m + 3n – 1).\nSolution\nKey Steps: • Group the terms.\n• Use the cross-method.\n•  Take out the common factor.\n4m^{2} – 7mn + 3n^{2} + m – n\n= (4m^{2} – 7mn + 3n^{2}) + (m – n)  → •\n= (4m – 3n)(m – n) + (m – n)  → •\n= (m – n)(4m – 3n + 1)  → →\n∴ The answer is A.",
     "h^{2} – 3h – 4k^{2} – 6k =\nA. (h – 2k)(h – 2k + 3).\nB. (h – 2k)(h + 2k + 3).\nC. (h + 2k)(h – 2k – 3).\nD. (h + 2k)(h + 2k – 3).\nSolution\nKey Steps: • Group the terms.\n• Use a^{2} – b^{2} ≡ (a + b)(a – b).\n•  Take out the common factor.\nh^{2} – 3h – 4k^{2} – 6k\n= (h^{2} – 4k^{2}) – (3h + 6k)  → •\n= (h + 2k)(h – 2k) – 3(h + 2k)  → • and →\n= (h + 2k)(h – 2k – 3)  → →\n∴ The answer is C."
    ]
   ]
